  "overview": "The Micro is what you get if you shrink a Leonardo to Nano-sized proportions: the same ATmega32U4 chip with native USB (so it can act as a USB keyboard/mouse/HID device), but in a breadboard-friendly board with male headers instead of the Uno/Leonardo's female sockets. It's the board to reach for when a project needs USB HID tricks in a tight space.",
